   "id": "e27",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 66,
   "y": 528,
   "width": 562.8000000000001,
   "height": 18.75,
   "text": "Where the intersection actually happens \u2014 worth being precise about",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "Where the intersection actually happens \u2014 worth being precise about",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "angle": 0,
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 222732,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 2934412,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "id": "e28",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 66,
   "y": 562,
   "width": 948.6400000000001,
   "height": 87.5,
   "text": "The AuthPolicy does NOT check the operator and the agent separately. It cannot: the token carries one role set, not two.\nKeycloak has already intersected them at step 2, so by the time Authorino sees the token, a role present in it means BOTH\nthe operator holds it AND the agent may be delegated it. Same guarantee, enforced one hop earlier \u2014 and the reason no\nAuthPolicy change is needed. The flip side: if fullScopeAllowed were ever set back to true, the agent-side limit would\nsilently disappear and the policy would not notice. That boolean is load-bearing.",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "The AuthPolicy does NOT check the operator and the agent separately. It cannot: the token carries one role set, not two.\nKeycloak has already intersected them at step 2, so by the time Authorino sees the token, a role present in it means BOTH\nthe operator holds it AND the agent may be delegated it. Same guarantee, enforced one hop earlier \u2014 and the reason no\nAuthPolicy change is needed. The flip side: if fullScopeAllowed were ever set back to true, the agent-side limit would\nsilently disappear and the policy would not notice. That boolean is load-bearing.",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
